-- Hand-written, not generated: the reference range of a vital sign for each age, and for a child's blood pressure each
-- sex (the expansion plan's steps 9b and 9d, Tahseen's decisions of 19 November 2026). Heart rate (8867-4) and
-- respiratory rate (9279-1): the 1st and 99th centiles of Fleming et al.'s 13 age groups, then the adults' range from
-- 18. Systolic and diastolic blood pressure (8480-6, 8462-4): the AAP guideline's Table 6 for each year of age from 1
-- to 12 and for 13 to 18, by sex, as printed, then the adults' range from 18; under 1 year there is none. Temperature
-- and oxygen saturation keep the one range ehr.observation_codes gives them. Ages are whole months: from from_months,
-- up to but not including to_months.
--
-- A 'normal' row flags a value below low or above high; an end that no source gives is NULL. A 'screening' row (a
-- child's blood pressure) is a value at or above which a reading needs follow-up: the table is for screening only, so
-- such a reading is never called abnormal. A patient whose sex is other or unknown is held to the lower of the boys'
-- and girls' values (ehr.file_result). Each row names its source and the page its numbers are on; what each source
-- defines, and what was decided, are in docs/expansion/reference-data.md. They are for flagging synthetic values on a
-- flowsheet and are not validated for clinical use.
--
-- The same rows are Ehr.Data.Reference.VitalRanges, which the seed uses; a test fails if the two differ, and another
-- holds both to a copy of the published tables. Applied as ehr_owner after db/policies and after 30-observations.sql,
-- whose codes it refers to; safe to run again: it makes the table hold exactly these rows.
BEGIN;
CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE incoming_vital_ranges (code text, sex text, from_months int, to_months int, low numeric, high numeric, kind text, source text) ON COMMIT DROP;
